WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.140
Chapter 1 asked of any pile: how fast does it arrive, and how fast does it leave?

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.960
Now ask that inside the ER.

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.720
What happens when unfinished proteins arrive faster than the ER can fold or remove

4
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.720
them?

5
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:23.793
Many secreted and membrane protein chains enter the ER through a channel called the

6
00:00:23.793 --> 00:00:27.293
translocon. Chaperones then help them fold.

7
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:31.073
BiP grips exposed hydrophobic stretches.

8
00:00:32.593 --> 00:00:38.073
Lectin chaperones read sugar tags on many glycoproteins, supporting repeated folding

9
00:00:38.073 --> 00:00:41.893
attempts. Folded clients can leave for the Golgi.

10
00:00:43.333 --> 00:00:49.413
Some persistently misfolded clients enter ER-associated degradation, or ERAD.

11
00:00:50.653 --> 00:00:55.753
During return toward the cytosol, yeast Hrd1 adds a ubiquitin chain.

12
00:00:57.393 --> 00:01:02.133
Cdc48 extracts the tagged client for destruction by the proteasome.

13
00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.467
Now count the flows.

14
00:01:06.007 --> 00:01:08.087
Arrival is ER-destined chains entering.

15
00:01:09.327 --> 00:01:12.887
Clearance is folding and export, plus removal by ERAD.

16
00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:19.567
When chains arrive faster than both exits can take them, unfolded proteins build up.

17
00:01:20.687 --> 00:01:23.627
The ER senses that stress and raises an alarm.

18
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.757
This alarm is the unfolded protein response.

19
00:01:29.137 --> 00:01:30.137
Look at the equation.

20
00:01:31.337 --> 00:01:34.277
Which flows could the response change to bring the load down?

21
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.490
It can change both sides.

22
00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:47.590
In mammals, a sensor called PERK slows the making of most new proteins, so less

23
00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:53.470
arrives. The response also increases folding helpers and removal machinery.

24
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.650
Less in and more out let the load fall.

25
00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.480
Mammals have three branches.

26
00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.200
IRE1 splices the XBP1 message.

27
00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.760
PERK slows translation.

28
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.900
ATF6 travels to the Golgi, where proteases release its transcription factor domain.

29
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:18.400
Yeast relies on one ER-stress sensor, Ire1.

30
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.880
The response buys time, but has limits.

31
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.860
Persistent stress can also drive cell death.

32
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.880
The ER can retry clients, remove them, slow arrival, or raise capacity.

33
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.460
These moves rebalance arrival and clearance.

34
00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.760
When folding falls behind, reduce arrival and expand capacity.
